Tribonacci sequence.\n    The sequence follows a specific recurrence relation including base cases and rules for even and odd numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    _memo: dict[int, int] = {}\n\n    def _get_single_tri_value(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Recursively computes a single Tribonacci value for index k with memoization.\"\"\"\n        if k in _memo:\n            return _memo[k]\n\n        if k == 0:\n            value = 1\n        elif k == 1:\n            value = 3\n        elif k % 2 == 0:  # k is even and k > 0\n            value = 1 + k // 2\n        else:  # k is odd and k > 1\n            value = _get_single_tri_value(k - 1) + _get_single_tri_value(k - 2) + _get_single_tri_value(k + 1)\n\n        _memo[k] = value\n        return value\n\n    result_sequence: list[int] = []\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        result_sequence.append(_get_single_tri_value(i))\n\n    return result_sequence\n```", "base_status": "fail", "plus_status": "fail", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}, {"task_id": "HumanEval/130", "solution": "```python\ndef tri(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Tribonacci sequence up to tri(n) using dynamic programming.\n    Handles base cases and recurrence relations for even and odd indices.\"\"\"\n\n    # Initialize array to store Tribonacci values up to n+1 for dependency tri(n+1).\n    # The size is n+2 as indices go from 0 to n+1.\n    trib_values = [0] * (n + 2)\n\n    # FR3: Calculate Base Case tri(0)\n    trib_values[0] = 1\n\n    # FR4: Calculate Base Case tri(1) if n allows\n    if n >= 1:\n        trib_values[1] = 3\n\n    # FR5: Calculate Even-Indexed Tribonacci Numbers first.\n    # This loop ensures tri(i+1) is available for odd-indexed calculations.\n    for i in range(2, n + 2):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # If i is an even integer greater than 0\n            trib_values[i] = 1 + i // 2\n\n    # FR6: Calculate Odd-Indexed Tribonacci Numbers.\n    # This loop uses already computed values for i-1, i-2, and i+1.\n    for i in range(3, n +